WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.663
Exercise 3 focuses on a boundary-safe case
expression You need

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:12.253
five outcomes missing exact zero High Value Standard
and Low Value The

00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:17.890
order matters Start with null Then handle exact

00:00:17.903 --> 00:00:23.452
zero After that check the ten-thousand threshold
Then

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:29.462
check the five-thousand threshold Finally use ELSE
for the remaining known values

00:00:31.273 --> 00:00:34.597
Complete the case expression in the browser and use
Run and Check

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:39.032
You can also copy the starter query into pgAdmin and
test it

00:00:39.058 --> 00:00:43.555
there I recommend testing a few values mentally
before you run the

00:00:43.568 --> 00:00:49.341
query Ask yourself where should zero go Where should
exactly five

00:00:49.354 --> 00:00:54.857
thousand go What about exactly ten thousand What
about null

00:00:55.759 --> 00:00:59.290
If those four cases are correct your boundaries are
probably in good

00:00:59.315 --> 00:00:59.715
shape
